 <longdesc><para unique="1091570">This instruction cannot be used for register to register or memory to memory moves.</para>
  <para unique="1091571">128-bit Legacy SSE load:</para>
  <para unique="1091572">Moves a double precision floating-point value from the source 64-bit memory operand and stores it in the low 64-bits of the destination XMM register. The upper 64bits of the XMM register are preserved. Bits (MAXVL-1:128) of the corresponding destination register are preserved.</para>
  <para unique="1091573">VEX.128 &amp; EVEX encoded load:</para>
  <para unique="1091574">Loads a double precision floating-point value from the source 64-bit memory operand (third operand), merges it with the upper 64-bits of the first source XMM register (second operand), and stores it in the low 128-bits of the destination XMM register (first operand). Bits (MAXVL-1:128) of the corresponding destination register are zeroed.</para>
  <para unique="1091575">128-bit store:</para>
  <para unique="1091576">Stores a double precision floating-point value from the low 64-bits of the XMM register source (second operand) to the 64-bit memory location (first operand).</para>
  <para unique="1091577">Note: VMOVLPD (store) (VEX.128.66.0F 13 /r) is legal and has the same behavior as the existing 66 0F 13 store. For VMOVLPD (store) VEX.vvvv and EVEX.vvvv are reserved and must be 1111b otherwise instruction will #UD.</para>
  <para unique="1091578">If VMOVLPD is encoded with VEX.L or EVEX.L&#8217;L= 1, an attempt to execute the instruction encoded with VEX.L or EVEX.L&#8217;L= 1 will cause an #UD exception.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1091580">MOVLPD (128-bit Legacy SSE Load)</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[63:0] := SRC[63:0]
DEST[MAXVL-1:64] (Unmodified)</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1091583">VMOVLPD (VEX.128 &amp; EVEX Encoded Load)</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[63:0] := SRC2[63:0]
DEST[127:64] := SRC1[127:64]
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1091588">VMOVLPD (Store)</title>
   <programlisting>DEST[63:0] := SRC[63:0]</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>MOVLPD __m128d _mm_loadl_pd ( __m128d a, double *p)
MOVLPD void _mm_storel_pd (double *p, __m128d a)</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1091594">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1091599" format="xIndent1">Non-EVEX-encoded instruction, see <link unique="1091597" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#48385: 06_Table: Table 2-22. Type 5 Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-comma">Table&#160;2&#8209;22, &#8220;Type 5 Class Exception Conditions,&#8221;</link> additionally:</para>
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1091600">If VEX.L = 1.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  <para unique="1091604" format="xIndent1">EVEX-encoded instruction, see <link unique="1091602" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#32485: 06_Table: Table 2-57. Type E9NF Class Exception Conditions" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-period">Table&#160;2&#8209;59, &#8220;Type E9NF Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
